From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sigivb72-netizen <vergilx63@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:50:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] podot: core: in-process instances and a re-entrant engine
 core

Platforms that cannot spawn processes (the iPadOS editor) can enable
in-process instances: OS::create_instance() queues the arguments, and the
platform main loop cleans up Main and sets it up again with them. A small
OS key/value store survives these relaunches.

Making Main::setup() work again after Main::cleanup():
- StringName: keep the entries referenced by static StringNames (SNAME).
- GDCLASS/Object: register classes once per ClassDB generation (a static
  "initialized" flag and the static GDType pointer survived cleanup).
- ObjectDB: reset the slot table after freeing it.
- Main: reset file-scope state, benchmark marks and iteration state.
- CompositeLogger: drop the loggers added by Main on cleanup.
- Core singletons clear their pointer when destroyed (ResourceUID,
  TranslationServer, ZipArchive, IP, MIDIDriver, resource formats, ...).

linuxbsd honors GODOT_IN_PROCESS_INSTANCES=1, to test the flow on desktop.

Touch canvas gestures: TouchGestureRecognizer turns raw touches into
drawing-app style navigation (two-finger drag -> InputEventPanGesture,
pinch -> InputEventMagnifyGesture, two/three-finger taps -> undo/redo
callback), holding the first touch back briefly so that a gesture never
also produces single-finger input. New project settings
input_devices/pointing/ios/enable_pan_and_scale_gestures and
input_devices/pointing/ios/pencil_as_mouse.

Fix: Input dispatched every gesture event twice (pinch and trackpad pan
were applied twice on all platforms).

Main::iteration() steps a game running inside the editor process
(InProcessGame) after the editor's frame, with physics callbacks in game
mode. TouchGestureRecognizer: touches starting in a direct-input area (the
game window) are delivered immediately and never become gestures.
